      "body": "## Problem\n\nThe DSV4 CUDA Cluster top-k path still caps each rank's threshold-bin candidate count at 2048 before aggregating it on rank 0. When the actual bin is larger, the kernel silently selects from an arrival-order subset and can miss true top-k scores. PR #37941 made the Register and Streaming paths exact, but left the Cluster path unchanged. Related: #35257.\n\n## Change\n\n- Preserve uncapped threshold-bin counts across Cluster ranks while keeping writes to the fixed tie buffer bounded.\n- If the aggregate overflows the buffer, rerun the full row on rank 0 through the existing exact Streaming path. Cluster barriers keep peer shared memory valid until the retry finishes.\n- Exercise both the small-batch and persistent Cluster launch shapes with concentrated fp32 scores and compare the selected score multiset against `torch.topk`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check` and Python syntax compilation passed.\n- An earlier H20 test of this Cluster fallback combined with #37941 removed strict top-k misses on long rows. This draft is rebased onto current main; GPU CI for this exact branch is still pending.\n- No CUDA device is available in the local development environment, so the added GPU tests have not been run here.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41031078007](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41031078007)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41031077965](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41031077965)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41031078001](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41031078001)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
